{
  "meta": {
    "title": "mail no-timing toy: forcing eviction, firing deadlines and reading alarms instead of waiting, on local workerd",
    "status": "done",
    "date": "2026-11-05",
    "author": "platform",
    "track": "mail testing"
  },
  "finding": "Mail's tests can stop waiting: workerd:unsafe's evict with hibernate reproduces the runtime's eviction field for field, deadlines behind a port can be fired by the test, and a stored alarm survives a kill and can be read and fired, which cut the auth toy's workerd suite from 746 s to 155 s; ctx.abort() is not eviction, because it drops the socket.",
  "premise": "Can tests control time instead of measuring it, so no test passes or fails on how long something took?",
  "provenance": {
    "source_workflow": "One general-purpose agent on local workerd and Node, reusing the auth and storage toys, 5 predictions recorded first (01a1adfd-b68a to 01a1adfd-b6c6), all witnessed.",
    "method": "Test-only routes into the real session object, constructor counters, memory tokens, row and socket checks, the runtime's own 25 s eviction as a control, SIGKILL of the process tree, node mock.timers.",
    "verification": {
      "claims_held": 5,
      "refuted": 1,
      "unverifiable": 1
    },
    "tool_limits": "Local workerd only: production eviction, module scope across eviction, and whether a forced eviction mid-handler means anything are unknown. Reading mail-main was denied, so which timer mail uses for these closes was not checked."
  },
  "claims": [
    {
      "claim": "workerd:unsafe evict(stub, { webSockets: 'hibernate' }) from a test-only route, with compatibility flag unsafe_module and a variable-specifier import(): a selected session answered FETCH from saved state 5 of 5 with the constructor rerun, rows identical and socket open; before login the alarm stayed and LOGIN was answered 5 of 5. The runtime's own 25 s eviction matched on every field (n=4). webSockets: 'close' dropped the socket 5 of 5",
      "status": "verified",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "toy-notime",
        "locator": "toy-notime/results/"
      }
    },
    {
      "claim": "After SIGKILL of the whole tree and a restart on the same state, the stored alarm read back identical before it was due, 3 of 3; moving it to now fired it and ended the object about 6 ms later. Shown on an idle session's greeting alarm, not a mailbox mid-erase",
      "status": "verified",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "toy-notime",
        "locator": "toy-notime/results/"
      }
    },
    {
      "claim": "Node under mock.timers: open at 9999 ms, closed 1011 with no NO at 10000 ms, two tests in 0.17 s. workerd 5 of 5: the test read the requested 60000 ms deadline and fired it, each socket closed 1011 with no NO, run 0.22 s. The close reason is empty on the wire, the submission half and the fake seeing the close were not shown",
      "status": "verified",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "toy-notime",
        "locator": "toy-notime/results/"
      }
    },
    {
      "claim": "746 s to 155 s, 79 percent less, same outcomes test by test, n=1 each. About 50 s is still real: a 10 s poll for a refusal that never comes, five times; about 57 s is in tests that measure timing on purpose",
      "status": "verified",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "toy-notime",
        "locator": "toy-notime/results/"
      }
    },
    {
      "claim": "ctx.abort() can stand in for eviction in a test.",
      "status": "refuted",
      "is_self_correction": true,
      "evidence": {
        "source": "toy-notime",
        "locator": "toy-notime/results/",
        "text": "ctx.abort() reran the constructor and kept storage but dropped the socket 5 of 5: the next FETCH got EOF, and the session's rows were orphaned because #end never ran"
      }
    },
    {
      "claim": "createTestHarness().getWorker().evictDurableObject() and abortAllDurableObjects do the same as evict.",
      "status": "unverified",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "toy-notime",
        "locator": "toy-notime/results/",
        "text": "Read in source only, not run."
      }
    }
  ],
  "caveats": [
    "Module scope survived both kinds of eviction locally; production is unknown, so tests must not rely on it.",
    "A test route reaching an object by id works locally because the Worker and the object share an isolate.",
    "Evict only after the last reply is read: evicting mid-handler tests something production never does.",
    "Reading an alarm is itself a call to the object, which FR-MAIL-053-c13 says a resume must not need.",
    "Still real time: waiting on wrangler's file watcher (an event, not a set time), proving a refusal never comes, timing measurements, and production eviction."
  ],
  "body": {
    "helpers": {
      "evictSession": "evictSession(id: string): Promise<void> // evict(stub, { webSockets: 'hibernate' }); test config only, compatibility flag unsafe_module",
      "Deadline": "type Deadline = (ms: number, reason: string) => Promise<never> // real: setTimeout; test: held(owner)",
      "pending and expire": "pending(owner): { ms; reason }[]; expire(owner): { ms; reason }[] // fired inside the object",
      "alarms": "alarmAt(id): Promise<number | null>; alarmNow(id): Promise<number | null>"
    },
    "must_hold": [
      "The 10 s tell bound in imap-objects.ts (bounded) calls setTimeout directly and needs the Deadline port.",
      "An adapter that aborts by signal needs the port to hand out a signal as well."
    ],
    "code": "scratchpad/toy-notime (src/index.ts, src/clock.ts, client/, node-test/, results/, logs/) in session d1068c98-86bb-4fa2-8415-63ac37e80e78"
  }
}
